I've had no problem with the binaries.  I uudecoded them on my Unix machine
and downloaded the .exe's.  Everything worked fine.  

I do have other beefs though.  I had the dungeon collapse on me twice.  This
has never happened to me before during any of my nethack games.  Maybe I was
lucky before and my luck just ran out, but I still find it strange.  I also
noticed, that for the first time, the Medusa was in a room filled with
soldiers.  None of them had blindfolds with them.  How is this possible?  Am
I missing something?  There were a good 20-30 soldiers in there (dlvl 25) and
I had to kill most of them before I could stone the Medusa.  Later I
polymorphed a pile of stuff and when trying to pick up "a polished shield", the
dungeon collapsed, with some error message. (I'll get the # next time).  This
happened twice.  Has anybody else seen this ?


On another note Dave Hairston was asking about what an Oracle could possibly 
add to the dungeon environment.  I think you should be able to ask a question
of some sort (for the appropriate amount of zorkmids of course).  Sort of like
this :

(You approach the Oracle) #chat
(now give the direction)  "The Oracle wants to know what you ask about"
(You answer)		     : unicorns     
(The Oracle answers)      :"They say that unicorns are fond of jems"
(You owe the Oracle 50 zorkmids)
(You refuse to pay)
(You see 50 Keystone Kops appear next to you)
(You decide to pay)

This way the Oracle can be used as a source of information relevant to 
your present action.  The way it is now, the Oracle supplies info that is
usually not new.


Just an idea.  I have more.  Let's hear your's, Dave.
